<article class="env-definition" id="07XF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07XF">Definition <span data-tag="07XF">98.12.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a locally Noetherian scheme. Let $\mathcal{X}$ be fibred in groupoids over $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$. Let $U$ be a scheme locally of finite type over $S$. Let $x$ be an object of $\mathcal{X}$ lying over $U$. Let $u_0$ be a finite type point of $U$. We say $x$ is <em>versal</em> at $u_0$ if the morphism $\hat x$ (<a href="/tag/07XE" data-tag="07XE">98.12.1.1</a>) is smooth, see Formal Deformation Theory, Definition <a href="/tag/06HG" data-tag="06HG">90.8.1</a>. </p>
</article>